			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SHAPE RENDER\n\nThe Shape render will render the Shape2D type to a Texture2Drgba type.\nThis means that you are translating the shapes into pixels.\nKeep in mind that this is a one-way conversion.\nYou can convert shapes into texture, but not textures into shapes.\n\nYou can set the amount of antialiasing in the Shape Render node.\nThis allows you to render the shape with soft edges  (and can provide really cheap blurs in some situations).\n\nA Camera2D node can be connected to the Shape Render node to zoom and pan the shape."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 260.21868896484375,
					"width": 675.28924560546875,
					"x": 124.4720306396484375,
					"y": 74.031982421875
				},
				"class": {
